      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the structure. The test has several issues affecting understandability:\n1. Many unused imports and unused data provider methods that add noise\n2. The assertions lack organization — it's hard to see which rule each year is testing\n3. No inline grouping comments\n\nI'll write an improved version that removes the clutter, keeps only what's needed, and groups assertions by the Pax leap year rule they exercise.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports and unused data provider methods, then organizes the assertions into clearly labeled groups that map each test case to the specific Pax leap year rule it exercises, making the test's intent immediately obvious to any reader."
